WEBVTT

1
00:53:32.098 --> 00:53:42.598
It is for the Dutch school holiday, it is the end of the holiday. The children will go back to school on Monday or Tuesday.

2
00:53:42.598 --> 00:53:55.098
Dutch teenagers, when are you going back to school? Tuesday? Is anyone happy about that? No? God bless you.

3
00:53:55.098 --> 00:53:59.098
They say that school is the best time of your life.

4
00:53:59.098 --> 00:54:04.098
And the Bible says that you should not lie, so we will not lie about that either. That is simply not true at all.

5
00:54:04.098 --> 00:54:09.098
It is not the most fun time of your life. Praise the Lord.

6
00:54:09.098 --> 00:54:16.098
Youth camps are indeed the best time of your life. Can I get an amen on that?

7
00:54:16.098 --> 00:54:21.098
We really had a great time. Is Fonja in the room? Fonja is not in the room, right?

8
00:54:21.098 --> 00:54:28.098
Which other children's leader is in the room? Children's leaders, please stand up. All children's leaders from the children's camp, please stand up.

9
00:54:28.098 --> 00:54:38.098
Awesome, awesome, awesome, awesome. Amazing, amazing.

10
00:54:39.098 --> 00:54:44.098
Feebe, come here. Feebe, come here. Can I get a round of applause for Feebe?

11
00:54:49.098 --> 00:54:53.098
Feebe, tell us something. Share a testimony about the children's camp.

12
00:54:53.098 --> 00:55:02.098
At the children's camp, we were allowed to teach the children about their identity, who they are in Jesus and what Jesus says about them.

13
00:55:02.098 --> 00:55:11.098
And we had a very nice exercise where the children had words that are not nice, which the world sometimes speaks over them.

14
00:55:11.098 --> 00:55:17.098
And the children were also allowed to indicate what they have felt at times.

15
00:55:17.098 --> 00:55:25.098
And there were words like ugly, unwanted, not good enough, excluded.

16
00:55:25.098 --> 00:55:40.098
Really all the children's leaders, I think I speak on behalf of all of us, it truly broke our hearts to see that even at such a young age children already have such feelings, can feel so ordinary.

17
00:55:40.098 --> 00:55:46.098
And it was so beautiful that we were allowed to plant the truth in them.

18
00:55:46.098 --> 00:55:56.098
We were able to say, you know, you are not ugly because God made you beautiful, you are a child of God, you are loved by God.

19
00:55:56.098 --> 00:56:03.098
So it was really beautiful to be able to plant the truth in the lives of these children.

20
00:56:04.098 --> 00:56:10.098
APPLAUSE

21
00:56:10.098 --> 00:56:13.098
It was just amazing.

22
00:56:13.098 --> 00:56:21.098
My daughter came home and in the evening we put them to bed, those kids are wrecked, really.

23
00:56:21.098 --> 00:56:26.098
Had a nice time, but they are dirty and tired.

24
00:56:27.098 --> 00:56:32.098
So wonderful. And Olivia, she is really such a nostalgic child.

25
00:56:32.098 --> 00:56:36.098
Crying boy, crying. I want to go back to camp, I want to go back to camp.

26
00:56:36.098 --> 00:56:40.098
And such a beautiful time that those children had.

27
00:56:40.098 --> 00:56:45.098
And the worship among the children, it is just really genuine worship.

28
00:56:45.098 --> 00:56:50.098
So it's not just, oh nice. No, they are truly engaged in worship.

29
00:56:51.098 --> 00:56:55.098
And suddenly Olivia crying, crying. And we are like, girl you are just tired.

30
00:56:55.098 --> 00:56:57.098
No, no, I'm not tired.

31
00:56:57.098 --> 00:56:59.098
LAUGHTER

32
00:56:59.098 --> 00:57:01.098
Bam.

33
00:57:01.098 --> 00:57:03.098
Wonderful.

34
00:57:03.098 --> 00:57:13.098
Praise the Lord. And then, for those who don't know yet, in Openkerk we celebrate the children's camp from Sunday afternoon to Wednesday morning.

35
00:57:13.098 --> 00:57:19.098
And we tidy up that same camp location. Small adjustments.

36
00:57:19.098 --> 00:57:24.098
And then from Wednesday afternoon to Saturday morning it is the youth camp.

37
00:57:24.098 --> 00:57:28.098
And really, it was just another beautiful camp.

38
00:57:28.098 --> 00:57:33.098
All youth leaders, please stand up who were present at the youth camp.

39
00:57:33.098 --> 00:57:38.098
Youth leaders, amazing. Can I have a round of applause for these youth leaders.

40
00:57:38.098 --> 00:57:40.098
APPLAUSE

41
00:57:40.098 --> 00:57:43.098
Praise the Lord.

42
00:57:43.098 --> 00:57:48.098
Youth leaders, you may take a seat for a moment, as the youth themselves are present here.

43
00:57:48.098 --> 00:57:56.098
So may I please have a testimony from one of the young people here on stage about what you have learned.

44
00:57:56.098 --> 00:57:59.098
In five seconds, I will point someone out.

45
00:57:59.098 --> 00:58:02.098
Daniel, here is a volunteer, Daniel.

46
00:58:02.098 --> 00:58:04.098
APPLAUSE

47
00:58:04.098 --> 00:58:16.098
Daniel, if I were to ask you, what have you learned or what have you experienced with God at the youth camp?

48
00:58:16.098 --> 00:58:25.098
What I have experienced is, for a long time I have heard from everyone about the Holy Spirit.

49
00:58:25.098 --> 00:58:29.098
But I personally have not really experienced that yet.

50
00:58:29.098 --> 00:58:35.098
But at this youth camp, it was really immediate and overwhelming. I had goosebumps, I felt everything.

51
00:58:35.098 --> 00:58:41.098
APPLAUSE

52
00:58:41.098 --> 00:58:47.098
So what we sing here about tradition and religion.

53
00:58:47.098 --> 00:58:53.098
That I followed those rules blindly my whole life, but did not experience it myself.

54
00:58:54.098 --> 00:58:59.098
But I have finally been able to experience that now, and it is amazing.

55
00:58:59.098 --> 00:59:06.098
APPLAUSE

56
00:59:06.098 --> 00:59:11.098
And once again, truly. We provide teaching.

57
00:59:11.098 --> 00:59:16.098
I have made it a tradition over the past five, six, seven, eight years.

58
00:59:16.098 --> 00:59:18.098
I no longer know how many times we have done this.

59
00:59:18.098 --> 00:59:24.098
To give a summary sermon about the camp at the end of the camp.

60
00:59:24.098 --> 00:59:28.098
Maybe some teenagers think, yes, I have already heard that. Yes, that is correct, you have already heard that.

61
00:59:28.098 --> 00:59:32.098
We talked about that last week. But there is power in repetition. Amen.

62
00:59:32.098 --> 00:59:36.098
And I also find it nice that we can share this with the whole audience.

63
00:59:36.098 --> 00:59:39.098
Because this is not just a youth sermon, this is a church sermon. Amen.

64
00:59:39.098 --> 00:59:44.098
But at the end of the camp, I made that invitation.

65
00:59:44.098 --> 00:59:48.098
Listen, then we are going to bless everyone. Everyone will have hands laid on them.

66
00:59:48.098 --> 00:59:51.098
The teenagers who are up for it, they will have hands laid on them.

67
00:59:51.098 --> 00:59:54.098
And the teenagers who are not up for it, they will also have hands laid on them.

68
00:59:54.098 --> 00:59:57.098
Even extra long.

69
00:59:57.098 --> 01:00:01.098
But it was such a beautiful time. It was such a beautiful time.

70
01:00:01.098 --> 01:00:04.098
And you know, I fall for a very silly trap every time.

71
01:00:04.098 --> 01:00:09.098
Every time I fall for something that is so foolish in me.

72
01:00:10.098 --> 01:00:15.098
And this means this. Every camp week, on Wednesday evening, when it starts.

73
01:00:15.098 --> 01:00:19.098
Then I start with a piece of teaching and then, I dive right in.

74
01:00:19.098 --> 01:00:24.098
And then I always come home and think, ah yes, okay, a bit calmer.

75
01:00:24.098 --> 01:00:29.098
It's a slightly calmer camp and then I'm making excuses for myself.

76
01:00:29.098 --> 01:00:34.098
Why it was a bit calmer and why the teenagers might be waiting and so on.

77
01:00:34.098 --> 01:00:37.098
But it's purely my own flesh that judges that.

78
01:00:37.098 --> 01:00:41.098
What do I know? What do I know about what God is doing?

79
01:00:41.098 --> 01:00:44.098
But I judge that, but I shouldn't judge anything at all.

80
01:00:44.098 --> 01:00:51.098
And then you see that throughout the camp and then that last evening, the dedication and a simple question.

81
01:00:51.098 --> 01:00:53.098
Who wants to give their heart to Jesus?

82
01:00:53.098 --> 01:00:57.098
And seriously, I thought seriously with my fleshly, rational thought.

83
01:00:57.098 --> 01:01:02.098
I thought, yes, maybe five children, maybe four teenagers, maybe a few will come forward.

84
01:01:02.098 --> 01:01:06.098
Boom, one hundred percent came forward to give their heart to Jesus.

85
01:01:06.098 --> 01:01:11.098
And I bless you teenagers in the name of Jesus that the blood of Jesus will be alive in you.

86
01:01:11.098 --> 01:01:18.098
That the seed that was sown in you during the last camp cannot be stolen by Satan.

87
01:01:18.098 --> 01:01:22.098
For one thing is certain, Satan is indeed after you.

88
01:01:22.098 --> 01:01:26.098
And he will trouble you, both at your school and among your friends.

89
01:01:26.098 --> 01:01:29.098
But that is why the blood of Jesus is so important.

90
01:01:29.098 --> 01:01:34.098
And that is also why the protection of the church is so important, so that we can be together in our faith.

91
01:01:34.098 --> 01:01:40.098
Never give up again, in the name of Jesus. Amen.

92
01:01:40.098 --> 01:01:41.098
Amen.

93
01:01:41.098 --> 01:01:42.098
Praise name.

94
01:01:47.098 --> 01:01:50.098
Jeroen Elfrink is not here today, is he?

95
01:01:50.098 --> 01:01:53.098
No, he is not here, otherwise I would have heard him long ago.

96
01:01:54.098 --> 01:01:55.098
Amen!

97
01:01:55.098 --> 01:01:57.098
Ah yes, hi Jeroen.

98
01:01:57.098 --> 01:02:01.098
He can say amen so loudly that you can hear it in Ukraine even.

99
01:02:03.098 --> 01:02:05.098
Because he, why do I mention this?

100
01:02:05.098 --> 01:02:10.098
Remarkably enough, there was also a camp in Ukraine last week.

101
01:02:10.098 --> 01:02:15.098
And Jeroen Elfrink is one of us, but he is one of our missionaries.

102
01:02:15.098 --> 01:02:19.098
Jeroen Elfrink just can't sit still, he is completely crazy.

103
01:02:19.098 --> 01:02:24.098
And he never sits still and he travels back and forth all over Europe.

104
01:02:24.098 --> 01:02:30.098
To break God's Word and to set up events and to organize camps.

105
01:02:30.098 --> 01:02:35.098
And now for the second or third year, I think the second year, I could be wrong, second year.

106
01:02:35.098 --> 01:02:40.098
They are organizing it in Odessa, I think, Odessa, Ukraine.

107
01:02:40.098 --> 01:02:48.098
There they are organizing a camp and the invitation is specifically for teenagers and children.

108
01:02:48.098 --> 01:02:52.098
Whose parents have died at the front line.

109
01:02:52.098 --> 01:02:57.098
The reason is super intense, these children walk around with a backpack that makes you afraid.

110
01:02:57.098 --> 01:03:01.098
And there they also hold a youth camp.

111
01:03:01.098 --> 01:03:05.098
Last week while we were holding a camp, they were also holding a camp there.

112
01:03:05.098 --> 01:03:12.098
And last year we were able to donate 2,500 euros to them, because they simply needed it.

113
01:03:12.098 --> 01:03:21.098
And this year Jeroen Elfrink sends us another message and he just says, instead of 2,500 euros he says we need 5,000 euros.

114
01:03:21.098 --> 01:03:24.098
Look, those who do not ask will not receive.

115
01:03:24.098 --> 01:03:32.098
Okay, and so Open Church, without us having held a collection for this, I want to thank Open Church for your faithful gifts,

116
01:03:32.098 --> 01:03:38.098
for the tithes you give, for the gifts you give, for the sacrifices you make time and again.

117
01:03:38.098 --> 01:03:44.098
Because of that we could just, hop, on impulse transfer 5,000 euros for this camp as well.

118
01:03:44.098 --> 01:03:48.098
Just the money they need, bam, we could transfer it.

119
01:03:49.098 --> 01:03:55.098
And as I said, these camps have eternal value.

120
01:03:55.098 --> 01:04:01.098
And so I also believe that what Jeroen has done in Ukraine has eternal value.

121
01:04:01.098 --> 01:04:06.098
There, teenagers can receive healing, there they can make a choice for King Jesus.

122
01:04:06.098 --> 01:04:11.098
And that is why it is so important that we all commit ourselves to God's kingdom. Amen?

123
01:04:11.098 --> 01:04:13.098
Chris, may I invite you?

124
01:04:18.098 --> 01:04:24.098
Hallelujah.

125
01:04:24.098 --> 01:04:28.098
I want to express my thanks once again.

126
01:04:28.098 --> 01:04:33.098
Some time ago, we were also able to hold a collection for the summer camps.

127
01:04:33.098 --> 01:04:37.098
And 2415 euros were raised there.

128
01:04:37.098 --> 01:04:39.098
Thank you all very much.

129
01:04:39.098 --> 01:04:43.098
That is such an investment in our young people.

130
01:04:44.098 --> 01:04:49.098
And some time ago, we were also able to collect for our building project together.

131
01:04:49.098 --> 01:04:54.098
And again, 3730 euros were raised there.

132
01:04:56.098 --> 01:04:58.098
Hallelujah.

133
01:04:58.098 --> 01:05:02.098
Oh, it is so beautiful when we are in worship again this morning.

134
01:05:02.098 --> 01:05:06.098
And when we see the power of the gospel.

135
01:05:06.098 --> 01:05:11.098
God's kingdom is built with power and not with nice words.

136
01:05:11.098 --> 01:05:15.098
The gospel is the power of God for the salvation of everyone who believes.

137
01:05:15.098 --> 01:05:17.098
If I say it in NBG terms.

138
01:05:17.098 --> 01:05:21.098
And the power of the gospel is the deliverance from everything itself.

139
01:05:21.098 --> 01:05:23.098
But relying on yourself.

140
01:05:23.098 --> 01:05:27.098
In other words, the gospel is the redemption from that sin.

141
01:05:27.098 --> 01:05:30.098
For it is the intention that we trust in God.

142
01:05:30.098 --> 01:05:35.098
And the power of the gospel gives the freedom to walk in obedience and in faith.

143
01:05:35.098 --> 01:05:39.098
It simply sets you free to be able to do that.

144
01:05:39.098 --> 01:05:42.098
Completely free to be able to do that. How beautiful is that?

145
01:05:42.098 --> 01:05:48.098
And the power of the gospel becomes visible when you obediently do what Jesus says.

146
01:05:48.098 --> 01:05:51.098
Then you show it.

147
01:05:51.098 --> 01:05:54.098
These gifts show that.

148
01:05:54.098 --> 01:05:56.098
Also beautiful.

149
01:05:56.098 --> 01:05:58.098
This is worship.

150
01:05:58.098 --> 01:06:00.098
But it is also a testimony.

151
01:06:00.098 --> 01:06:05.098
And the power of the gospel becomes visible when you trust in the Father.

152
01:06:06.098 --> 01:06:10.098
And therefore I have a beautiful text for today.

153
01:06:10.098 --> 01:06:14.098
I don't know if you can already grasp it. Wonderful.

154
01:06:14.098 --> 01:06:20.098
It says, God, our Father, who gives seed to the sower to sow.

155
01:06:20.098 --> 01:06:22.098
And also bread to eat.

156
01:06:22.098 --> 01:06:26.098
So God gives seed to the sower.

157
01:06:26.098 --> 01:06:31.098
And just as He will give seed to us, to you.

158
01:06:31.098 --> 01:06:37.098
And then He will continue to give more seed as we do this.

159
01:06:39.098 --> 01:06:46.098
And then besides that, He says, and He will also ensure that there is a harvest from your good deeds.

160
01:06:47.098 --> 01:06:51.098
This is truly a cycle that God has set in motion.

161
01:06:51.098 --> 01:06:56.098
Sowing, harvesting. Sowing in faith. Harvesting.

162
01:06:56.098 --> 01:06:59.098
And in that intervening time, there is also a piece of time.

163
01:06:59.098 --> 01:07:01.098
That is a piece of expectation.

164
01:07:01.098 --> 01:07:06.098
And what God wants to teach us is to trust in Him. That we expect from Him.

165
01:07:06.098 --> 01:07:10.098
So when we sow, which is sometimes difficult, which is not always easy,

166
01:07:10.098 --> 01:07:14.098
we trust that He will give even more seed.

167
01:07:14.098 --> 01:07:19.098
For if we can trust Him, He can also trust you when you do what He says.

168
01:07:19.098 --> 01:07:25.098
And the more He can trust you in that, the more our faith grows.

169
01:07:25.098 --> 01:07:30.098
Our trust towards Him, but He can also trust us more and more. How beautiful is that?

170
01:07:31.098 --> 01:07:38.098
And when you look, when a farmer sows, there is really that expectation, that there will be a harvest.

171
01:07:38.098 --> 01:07:40.098
And that farmer is busy with that.

172
01:07:40.098 --> 01:07:42.098
And so it should be for us as well.

173
01:07:42.098 --> 01:07:46.098
Not just, stop quickly for a moment, or just quickly transfer something.

174
01:07:46.098 --> 01:07:50.098
But you may really expect a harvest from that.

175
01:07:50.098 --> 01:07:54.098
And if we all do that, God will also give us more seed, as we have just read.

176
01:07:55.098 --> 01:08:00.098
And Paul really means with seed, among other things.

177
01:08:00.098 --> 01:08:06.098
Sometimes you may sow efforts, you may sow love, you may sow all sorts of things.

178
01:08:06.098 --> 01:08:08.098
But also money.

179
01:08:08.098 --> 01:08:11.098
And money is something that God has given us.

180
01:08:11.098 --> 01:08:14.098
For actually, everything is already His. He doesn't need our money at all.

181
01:08:14.098 --> 01:08:19.098
But when we bring back a piece of what He has already given us,

182
01:08:19.098 --> 01:08:23.098
then that is a relationship, a covenant relationship.

183
01:08:23.098 --> 01:08:27.098
And I want to encourage us to step into that, in faith.

184
01:08:27.098 --> 01:08:32.098
That today we may do so in all freedom, faith, obedience, and joy, for that is also beautiful.

185
01:08:32.098 --> 01:08:37.098
For a farmer does not sit grumpily waiting for his harvest.

186
01:08:37.098 --> 01:08:41.098
He is happy when he sees it coming up.

187
01:08:41.098 --> 01:08:43.098
And we may do that too.

188
01:08:43.098 --> 01:08:49.098
And let us make the power of the gospel, the power of God's kingdom, visible with this.

189
01:08:49.098 --> 01:08:51.098
There is so much we can do.

190
01:08:51.098 --> 01:08:53.098
There is so much we can do.

191
01:08:53.098 --> 01:08:55.098
And even if it seems so small.

192
01:08:55.098 --> 01:08:57.098
But if we all faithfully do that together,

193
01:08:57.098 --> 01:08:59.098
then it is to see what God can do.

194
01:08:59.098 --> 01:09:01.098
So if we bring back what is in our hand,

195
01:09:01.098 --> 01:09:05.098
then the good, good Father will bring what is in His hand.

196
01:09:05.098 --> 01:09:07.098
Then it is to see what God can do with it.

197
01:09:07.098 --> 01:09:12.098
Perhaps it is beautiful to stand and bring this as a worship offering to God.

198
01:09:12.098 --> 01:09:15.098
Thank you, Father, that you are so good.

199
01:09:15.098 --> 01:09:17.098
Lord, you are a generous God.

200
01:09:17.098 --> 01:09:19.098
Lord, you have given everything.

201
01:09:19.098 --> 01:09:23.098
You have done everything. You have paid a price that we could never pay.

202
01:09:23.098 --> 01:09:25.098
And you simply did that.

203
01:09:25.098 --> 01:09:27.098
Lord, he had so much trust in us.

204
01:09:27.098 --> 01:09:31.098
But it is also the intention to actually do something with that.

205
01:09:31.098 --> 01:09:34.098
Lord, and I pray for us, that we may grow in this.

206
01:09:34.098 --> 01:09:40.098
Lord, that we may let your kingdom mentality develop in us as Father,

207
01:09:40.098 --> 01:09:44.098
so that Jesus will be seen, even through our wallets.

208
01:09:44.098 --> 01:09:47.098
And I thank you for that, that you do it, in the name of King Jesus. Amen.

209
01:09:50.098 --> 01:09:51.098
Amen.

210
01:09:56.098 --> 01:09:58.098
Glory to God. Amen.

211
01:10:01.098 --> 01:10:12.098
In two weeks, on 31.08, we have a book market and an international food market.

212
01:10:12.098 --> 01:10:16.098
How many years ago were we there?

213
01:10:16.098 --> 01:10:18.098
Two or three? Three now?

214
01:10:18.098 --> 01:10:21.098
This will be the fourth. This will be the third.

215
01:10:21.098 --> 01:10:23.098
International food market.

216
01:10:23.098 --> 01:10:26.098
And so, I love food.

217
01:10:26.098 --> 01:10:28.098
And the Lord does too.

218
01:10:28.098 --> 01:10:32.098
And it is so nice to have that fellowship together.

219
01:10:32.098 --> 01:10:38.098
And as I look around the room, I see so many different internationals.

220
01:10:38.098 --> 01:10:41.098
And so many different nationalities.

221
01:10:41.098 --> 01:10:44.098
You don't just want to talk about that, you also want to eat from it. Amen.

222
01:10:44.098 --> 01:10:47.098
So 31.08, let's all be there.

223
01:10:47.098 --> 01:10:51.098
Then let's just enjoy being together afterwards. We'll just make it a celebration.

224
01:10:51.098 --> 01:10:55.098
Later, at the end of the service, there will be ice cream for everyone.

225
01:10:55.098 --> 01:10:58.098
So the ice cream truck will come here soon.

226
01:10:58.098 --> 01:11:01.098
And all the teenagers will get a free ice cream.

